QEMU riscv virt: allow-list the DesignWare I3C controller on the platform bus

The RISC-V `virt` machine refuses to instantiate arbitrary `-device` types on
its platform bus: each type must be added to `allowed_dynamic_sysbus_dev`, and
the modules must be selected into the `RISCV_VIRT` Kconfig so they are compiled
into `qemu-system-riscv64`. Two files change:

  * hw/riscv/virt.c   — include the DW I3C header and register TYPE_DW_I3C via
                        machine_class_allow_dynamic_sysbus_dev() in
                        virt_machine_class_init().
  * hw/riscv/Kconfig  — `select I3C` + `select DW_I3C` under config RISCV_VIRT.

After rebuilding qemu-system-riscv64, `-device 'dw.i3c,help'` lists the nine
DW I3C properties instead of "Device 'dw.i3c' not found", and the controller
can be attached to the platform-bus MMIO window (0x04000000) for the Zephyr
i3c_dw driver. See README Part 3 for the full build/attach flow.

This targets an extracted QEMU 11.0.0 release tarball
(https://download.qemu.org/); apply from the QEMU source tree top.

---

### hw/riscv/virt.c (modified)
diff --git a/hw/riscv/virt.c b/hw/riscv/virt.c
--- a/hw/riscv/virt.c
+++ b/hw/riscv/virt.c
@@ -58,6 +58,7 @@
 #include "qapi/qapi-visit-common.h"
 #include "hw/virtio/virtio-iommu.h"
 #include "hw/uefi/var-service-api.h"
+#include "hw/i3c/dw-i3c.h"
 
 /* KVM AIA only supports APLIC MSI. APLIC Wired is always emulated by QEMU. */
 static bool virt_use_kvm_aia_aplic_imsic(RISCVVirtAIAType aia_type)
@@ -1937,6 +1938,7 @@
 
     machine_class_allow_dynamic_sysbus_dev(mc, TYPE_RAMFB_DEVICE);
     machine_class_allow_dynamic_sysbus_dev(mc, TYPE_UEFI_VARS_SYSBUS);
+    machine_class_allow_dynamic_sysbus_dev(mc, TYPE_DW_I3C);
 #ifdef CONFIG_TPM
     machine_class_allow_dynamic_sysbus_dev(mc, TYPE_TPM_TIS_SYSBUS);
 #endif

### hw/riscv/Kconfig (modified)
diff --git a/hw/riscv/Kconfig b/hw/riscv/Kconfig
--- a/hw/riscv/Kconfig
+++ b/hw/riscv/Kconfig
@@ -68,5 +68,7 @@ config RISCV_VIRT
     select PLATFORM_BUS
     select ACPI
     select ACPI_PCI
+    select I3C
+    select DW_I3C
 
 config SHAKTI_C
